{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Comparing Thermal Simulation with Infrared Measurements.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Comparing Thermal Simulation with Infrared Measurements.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"comparing thermal simulation with infrared measurements comparing thermal simulation with infrared measurements","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Comparing Thermal Simulation with Infrared Measurements.md","fileName":"Comparing Thermal Simulation with Infrared Measurements.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Comparing Thermal Simulation with Infrared Measurements","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-14 00:55\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Thermal Model Verification and Sensitivity]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Thermal Model Verification and Sensitivity","Thermal Imaging Calibration","cosmolheattransfermodels.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Comparing Thermal Simulation with Infrared Measurements.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Comparing Thermal Simulation with Infrared Measurements.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"comparing thermal simulation with infrared measurements comparing thermal simulation with infrared measurements","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Comparing Thermal Simulation with Infrared Measurements.md","fileName":"Comparing Thermal Simulation with Infrared Measurements.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Comparing Thermal Simulation with Infrared Measurements","heading":"Comparing Thermal Simulation with Infrared Measurements","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Infrared validation compares simulated surface temperatures with thermal-camera observations made under matching geometry, initial temperature, ambient conditions, and elapsed times. Point histories and spatial patterns reveal different kinds of disagreement and should both be considered.\n\nCamera accuracy, pixel resolution, emissivity settings, reflections, and uncertain convection coefficients limit the comparison. Agreement within those bounds supports the modeled behavior, while mismatch can direct revisions to [[Thermal Imaging Calibration|measurement treatment]], properties, or boundary conditions.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Thermal Model Verification and Sensitivity","Thermal Imaging Calibration","cosmolheattransfermodels.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Comparing Thermal Simulation with Infrared Measurements.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Comparing Thermal Simulation with Infrared Measurements.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"comparing thermal simulation with infrared measurements comparing thermal simulation with infrared measurements","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Comparing Thermal Simulation with Infrared Measurements.md","fileName":"Comparing Thermal Simulation with Infrared Measurements.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Comparing Thermal Simulation with Infrared Measurements","heading":"References","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"[[cosmolheattransfermodels.pdf]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Thermal Model Verification and Sensitivity","Thermal Imaging Calibration","cosmolheattransfermodels.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""}]}